etosa 50 Versicolor 50 Virginica 50 This shows the dataset is balanced. 3. Correlation Analysis Correlation analysis measures the relationship between numerical variables. Example findings: Petal length and petal width have strong positive correlation. Sepal width has weaker correlation with other variables. Correlation values usually range from -1 to +1. 4. Summary Statistics by Class Statistics are calculated separately for each species. Example analysis: Average petal length for Setosa Average sepal width for Versicolor Average petal width for Virginica This helps identify differences between species."],"metadata":{"id":"IIUK7LGohl_I"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#**Q.3 In Air Quality data set which graph is used to perform multivariate analysis?**\n","\n","ANS:-\n","\n","For air quality data sets, which typically involve multiple pollutants ( CO) and meteorological factors (temperature, wind speed, humidity), several graphs are used to perform multivariate analysis to understand relationships, correlations, and paflerns. The most effective graphs for this purpose are:"],"metadata":{"id":"8w-bomJ2hvf8"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#**Q.4 In Wine quality data set can you do non graphical EDA ? Explain your answer.**\n","\n","ANS:-\n","\n","How to Perform Non-Graphical EDA on Wine Quality Data Using Python's pandas library, you can perform the following non-graphical techniques to understand the dataset (which includes features like fixed acidity, volatile acidity, residual sugar, pH, and alcohol):\n","\n","Example Non-Graphical Findings on Wine Data Based on the Wine Quality dataset, non-graphical techniques usually reveal:\n","\n","Colab paid products - Cancel contracts here"],"metadata":{"id":"NdjaxgZQh82-"}}]}